---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import PrivacyNote from "../../components/PrivacyNote.astro";
---

<SiteLayout title="About the reader" description="How to read, print, download, and understand the privacy and licensing boundaries of the PHIL 123 interactive textbook.">
  <main id="main-content" class="about site-width">
    <p class="eyebrow">About this edition</p>
    <h1>A philosophy reader built for judgment</h1>
    <p class="lede">The reader pairs sustained textbook prose with explicit views of arguments, primary sources, people, and intellectual traditions. Each layer is meant to return you to the text with a better question.</p>

    <div class="about-grid">
      <section>
        <h2>Four ways into a chapter</h2>
        <dl>
          <dt>First Read</dt>
          <dd>The complete canonical chapter, with the prose given room to work.</dd>
          <dt>Deep Read</dt>
          <dd>Arguments, objections, concepts, and judgment points attached to stable passages.</dd>
          <dt>Sources</dt>
          <dd>Primary texts, editions, quotations, and rights information used by the chapter.</dd>
          <dt>World</dt>
          <dd>Thinkers, traditions, historical settings, and conceptual relationships.</dd>
        </dl>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Copies you can keep</h2>
        <p>Each chapter has a print view designed for paper or the browser's “Save as PDF” option. It also has a self-contained HTML download for offline reading. Both copies retain the chapter's headings, sources, license, and canonical address.</p>

        <h2>What the site does not do</h2>
        <PrivacyNote />
        <p>The first release does not include analytics, student accounts, AI feedback, or persistent peer discussion. Course discussion and submitted work remain in Canvas.</p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <section class="license-block">
      <h2>Open licenses, stated precisely</h2>
      <p>Original textbook prose is licensed under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>. Site software is licensed under the MIT License. Original structured metadata is dedicated under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/">CC0 1.0</a>. Third-party texts, translations, and images retain the rights stated on their individual records.</p>
      <p><a href="/rights/">Read the rights and attribution ledger</a></p>
    </section>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .about { padding-block: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 7rem); }
  h1 { max-width: 17ch; margin: 0.5rem 0 1.2rem; font-size: clamp(2.7rem, 7vw, 5.4rem); font-weight: 500; line-height: 0.98; letter-spacing: -0.045em; }
  .lede { max-width: 52rem; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .about-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: clamp(2rem, 7vw, 7rem); margin-top: 4rem; }
  h2 { margin: 0 0 0.8rem; font-size: 1.65rem; font-weight: 500; }
  section h2:not(:first-child) { margin-top: 2.3rem; }
  dl { margin: 0; }
  dt { margin-top: 1rem; color: var(--rust-dark); font: 700 0.74rem/1.3 var(--sans); letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  dd { margin: 0.25rem 0 0; }
  .license-block { max-width: 58rem; margin-top: 4rem; padding-top: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .about-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
